#X text 1000 2760 One trailing fork per episode \, when the last lost device answers: enumeration has finished then \, so it catches an undetectable device knocked off in the same event (item 275)., f 62;
#X text 480 2650 The attempts go to err too \, because the menu-launched patch's console is tty1 \, which nobody reads. No del 2000: nothing forks before the fourth tick after a loss \, long after the syntax check quits. C-9, f 62;
#X obj 20 2460 t b b;
#X msg 20 2720 info u_present rewire-try;
#X obj 20 2790 s err;
#X msg 1560 2300 info u_present rewire-last;
#X obj 1560 2370 s err;
#X text 20 2900 The forks name themselves \, rewire-try for the eight scheduled and rewire-last for the trailing one \, as info: logged \, never drawn over a set (C-12 \, item 289)., f 62;
#X obj 1900 2760 f;
#X obj 1900 2820 t f f;
#X obj 2100 2880 + 1;
#X obj 1900 2880 mod \$4;
#X obj 1900 2940 select 0;
#X msg 1900 3000 sh wire-watch.sh;
#X obj 1900 3060 shell;
#X obj 1900 3120 print wire-watch;
#X text 2400 2760 The heartbeat for a device nothing ever lost \, like the Volca's interface plugged in late (item 285). The count is taken after the increment \, so the first fork lands on tick 8 \, outside the boot window. wire-watch.sh hashes the client names and runs wire.sh only when they change (ref/module/presence.md)., f 62;
#X obj 1000 2500 t b b;
#X msg 1000 2620 info u_present rewire-asked;
#X obj 1000 2680 s err;
#X text 2500 1520 A third fork \, the only one a person asks for: re-wire on the presence bus \, a Send line through u_inject since the phone's button went (2026-11-04) \, into the same sh wire.sh box. One fork per ask and no counter reset \, with its own name on err \, rewire-asked \, because all three converge on one box., f 62;
